- src/params.rs — all SPHINCS+ sha2-256f constants and SHA2 address offsets
- src/context.rs — SpxCtx struct with seeded SHA-256/512 states
- src/sha2.rs — SHA-256/512 incremental hashing, MGF1, seed_state
- src/address.rs — address manipulation (layer, tree, type, keypair, chain, hash, tree height/index)
- src/hash.rs — initialize_hash_function, prf_addr, gen_message_random, hash_message
- src/thash.rs — robust thash (SHA-256 for 1 block, SHA-512 for >1 block, with MGF1 bitmask)
- src/utils.rs — ull_to_bytes, u32_to_bytes, bytes_to_ull, compute_root
- src/wots.rs — WOTS chain generation, base_w, checksum, wots_pk_from_sig
- src/wotsx1.rs — wots_gen_leafx1 (WOTS leaf generation with optional signing)
- src/utilsx1.rs — wots_treehashx1, fors_treehashx1 (Merkle tree building)
- src/fors.rs — FORS sign/verify, leaf generation
- src/merkle.rs — merkle_sign, merkle_gen_root
- src/rng.rs — AES-256-CTR-DRBG (deterministic RNG matching the C rng.c)
- src/sign.rs — crypto_sign_keypair, crypto_sign, crypto_sign_open, etc.

Key design decisions:
- Used aes crate instead of OpenSSL for AES-256-ECB (byte-identical behavior, no system dependency)
- Address bytes accessed via unsafe pointer casts to match C's (unsigned char *)addr pattern
- All SHA-2 implemented from scratch matching the C reference (not using a library) to ensure identical behavior
- Borrow conflicts resolved with temporary copies where needed
